a minted folder resolves back to its path: ok
ancestors are minted too: ok
an ancestor resolves too: ok
a folder is named by its own id: ok
a file is named by its folder and its leaf: ok
the domain root names itself: ok
a file under an unresolved folder has no name: ok
the root resolves to the domain root: ok
an unknown id resolves to nothing: ok
a renamed folder keeps its id: ok
the renamed folder is the same folder: ok
a deleted folder resolves to nothing: ok
its deleted parent does too: ok
a corrupted entry does not resolve to another folder: ok
and a rebuild puts it right: ok
a lost index answers nothing rather than rebuilding itself: ok
a lost index is restored by a rebuild: ok
rebuild prunes entries for departed folders: ok
a rebuilt index recovers an escaped name: ok
a folder nested past any fixed cap resolves: ok
a cycle in the index answers nothing rather than looping: ok
